note top of "ores::iam::domain::entity_type_of"
Eleven free overloads, one per generated entity, each declared in that
entity's own header and returning its dispatch key (for example
"ores.iam.account"). Every call site spells entity_type_of(value), so the
key is the single source of truth for the generic history-diff request and
for the action registries. The two junction entities, account_role and
role_permission, declare no overload.
end note
note bottom of "ores::iam::domain::entity_type_of"
Every generated entity also gets a convert_to_table overload taking a
vector of the entity, in its *_table.hpp; an ostream operator in its
*_table_io.hpp; a convert_to_json overload in its *_json.hpp (account,
login_info, permission and role only); and an ostream operator in its
*_json_io.hpp. They are uniform boilerplate and are not drawn.
end note

