note top of "ores::eventing::domain::entity_event_traits"
Ten specialisations, one per entity event struct, each declared in that
entity's own eventing header. The automated pass skips template
declarations, so none of the ten appears. Each states a subject_prefix and
converts the generic entity_event_notification into the entity's own event;
the notification carries the key as raw JSON, and only the entity knows
which columns its key record holds, so from_notification reads the key with
rfl::json and leaves the key default-constructed when that read fails. The
prefixes are: iam.v1.account_contact_informations_events, iam.v1.accounts_events, iam.v1.account_types_events, iam.v1.login_info_events, iam.v1.permissions_events, iam.v1.roles_events, iam.v1.sessions_events, iam.v1.tenants_events, iam.v1.tenant_statuses_events, iam.v1.tenant_types_events.
end note

