note right of "ores::iam::service::auth_session_service"
Hand-written, and the component's only hand-written source
(src/service/auth_session_service.cpp). It is an in-process map from Bearer
token to domain session, and every method takes the private mutable mutex_,
so one instance is safe to share. Nothing is persisted and nothing is
evicted on a timer: a session stays until remove_session is called. It
holds no account or permission state, so it answers who a token belongs to
and not what that account may do. The class is exported
(ORES_IAM_API_EXPORT), so consumers link it rather than re-implement it.
end note

